---
// Area page: the old Hambleton district (Northallerton, Thirsk, Bedale, Stokesley, Easingwold and the villages).
// Named after its towns, which is what people search for: "Hambleton primary school" is a village school near Selby.
// Questions follow Google's suggestions (November 2026).
import AreaPage from '../components/AreaPage.astro';
import { loadArea } from '../lib/areas';
import { COUNCILS } from '../lib/engine';
import { pageOf } from '../lib/schoolpages';
import { NY_TERM_DATES } from '../lib/specs';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
const ny = COUNCILS['North Yorkshire'];
const all = loadArea('north-yorkshire.json');
const schools = all.filter((s) => s.district === 'Hambleton');
// the village school called Hambleton, in the Selby district
const village = all.find((s) => s.district === 'Selby' && /^Hambleton\b/.test(s.name));
const faqs: [string, string][] = [
  ['What is my catchment school in Northallerton?',
    `Put your postcode into the <a href="${url('')}">school catchment checker</a>. It tells you which primary school catchment area you’re in, and your chances at every primary school nearby, in Northallerton, Thirsk, Bedale, Stokesley, Easingwold and the villages. Most schools here have a catchment, but a few, mostly academies, free schools and faith schools, set their own rules.`],
  ['Is there a school catchment area map for Northallerton and Thirsk?',
    `Yes. North Yorkshire Council publishes a <a href="${ny.catchMap}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">school catchment area map</a> covering every school in the county. The checker uses the same map, so your postcode gives you the answer. Near a boundary? Check your exact address on the council’s map.`],
  ['How do school catchment areas work in North Yorkshire?',
    `North Yorkshire Council fills each school’s places in order: children in care, then approved medical or social need, then children in the catchment, then children of staff, then everyone else. Brothers and sisters, then distance, decide who goes first inside each group. <a href="${url('how-places-work/')}">How school catchment areas work</a> explains the queue.`],
  ['When do I apply for a Reception place for September 2027?',
    `Apply online to <a href="${ny.apply}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">North Yorkshire Council</a> by Friday 15 January 2027. You can name up to five primary schools, in the order you want them.`],
  ['When are primary school places announced?',
    'Offers go out on national offer day, Friday 16 April 2027, by email from the council.'],
  ['Can my child get into a school outside our catchment?',
    'Often. Most schools round Northallerton, Thirsk and Bedale took everyone who applied in recent years. Where a school was full, the council publishes how far the last place went, and the checker compares that with your distance.'],
  ['Which are the best primary schools in Northallerton and Thirsk?',
    'There’s no official ranking, so be wary of league tables. Ofsted is the fairest guide, alongside a visit. The checker shows each school’s latest Ofsted outcome, and the Outstanding schools are listed above.'],
  ['We’re a forces family moving to RAF Leeming or Topcliffe. Can we apply before we arrive?',
    `Yes. Under the national School Admissions Code, you can apply before you move, using your unit or quartering address, if you have an official letter confirming the posting. Send it with your application to <a href="${ny.apply}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">North Yorkshire Council</a>. Leeming RAF Community Primary and Alanbrooke Academy at Topcliffe both serve service families.`],
  ['We live in Stokesley or Hutton Rudby. Can we apply for a Middlesbrough or Stockton school?',
    'Yes. Apply to North Yorkshire Council, as the council where you live, and you can name schools run by other councils among your five. The checker only covers North Yorkshire and York schools, so check those councils’ own figures.'],
  ['When are the school term dates and holidays?',
    `Community and voluntary controlled schools follow <a href="${NY_TERM_DATES}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">North Yorkshire Council’s term and holiday dates</a>. Academies, free schools and voluntary aided schools can set their own, so check with the school.`],
  ...(village ? [[`Looking for Hambleton Primary School?`,
    `Hambleton Church of England Primary School is in the village of Hambleton, near Selby. See <a href="${url(`schools/${pageOf(village.urn)!.slug}/`)}">its catchment area and admissions</a>, or every <a href="${url('selby-primary-schools/')}">Selby primary school</a>.`] as [string, string]] : []),
  ['How do I find open days?',
    'Ask the school. Open the school in the checker for its phone number, email and website.'],
];
---
<AreaPage areaKey="hambleton"
  title="Northallerton primary school catchment areas, map and Ofsted · Yorkshire School Checker"
  description="Northallerton, Thirsk, Bedale and Stokesley primary school catchment areas: find your catchment school, which schools are hardest to get into, Ofsted ratings and the 2027 Reception dates."
  h1="Northallerton, Thirsk and Bedale primary schools and catchment areas"
  lede="Primary school catchment areas for every school in Northallerton, Thirsk, Bedale, Stokesley, Great Ayton and Easingwold, and the villages from the Dales to the North York Moors."
  area="Northallerton and Thirsk"
  schools={schools}
  groups={[{ label: 'In the old Hambleton district', note: `${schools.length} North Yorkshire Council primary and infant schools.`, schools }]}
  faqs={faqs}
/>
